id: pm-extension-scalar-validation
title: Validate contributed scalar flag values before extension handler dispatch
description: "A harmless echo fixture declares type bool but --enabled not-a-boolean reaches its handler as a string. Coercion preserves invalid input for later validation, yet current dynamic dispatch validates only allowed/required/disabled option keys. Establish an explicit compatible scalar-validation contract for extension authors."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-14T16:21:40.172Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-15T22:07:43.694Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-15T15:10:35.660Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-15T15:10:35.660Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: Define compatibility for invalid number/boolean tokens and optional no-value presence; Apply shared SDK-owned scalar validation before handler invocation where opted in or required by the supported contract; Preserve canonical switch positional behavior and legacy bool grammar; Independently assert malformed value refusals and valid coercion/default/list cases through public CLI/SDK
parent: pm-ugqx
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "FlagDefinition.value_validation (coerce default, strict) declared in extension-types, validated at registration (unknown policy and strict on string/untyped flags refused), and enforced before dispatch in the loose option coercer: malformed number/boolean tokens refuse with extension_flag_value_invalid naming flag, command, expected grammar and received token; list entries validated individually; switch presence, --no- negation, the legacy bool optional-value grammar and defaults preserved. Shared helper describeFlagScalarValueFailure exported through runtime-primitives."
expected_result: "Extension authors can declare scalar validation that rejects malformed boolean and numeric inputs before dispatch while preserving valid aliases, defaults, optional presence and list ordering across public SDK and CLI."
actual_result: "Post-fix run on 2026-10-16 through pm test --run after the PR #1479 review follow-ups (alias pre-validation, attached switch tokens, empty and CSV-empty strict list entries, plain-object option bags): linked unit and integration tests pass; the loose option coercer and extension-flag integration spec sit at 100 percent statement and branch coverage in the per-file report; CI coverage gate green on the last head."
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
